  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "SipRequestFirstLine::SipRequestFirstLine",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/SipLayer.cpp",
    "description": "The constructor calls parseVersion(), which represents an absent or truncated SIP version by setting m_VersionOffset to -1, but then unconditionally uses that offset in memchr at line 138. This forms m_Data + (-1), an out-of-bounds start pointer, while casting -1 to size_t makes the subtraction wrap to m_DataLen + 1. memchr consequently reads outside the packet buffer and crashes. The constructor must validate m_VersionOffset before doing pointer arithmetic/searching. UdpLayer admits the malformed request because it tests only whether the method is recognized.",
    "conditions": "A captured packet must parse as UDP with either endpoint on a SIP port, and its UDP payload must begin with a recognized SIP request method so UdpLayer constructs SipRequestLayer. If the bounded UDP payload does not contain a valid/complete version marker (for example, the marker lies beyond the declared payload length or the request line is truncated), parseVersion() leaves m_VersionOffset at -1. The supplied pcap reaches this path through FuzzTarget's pcap reader and Packet parsing, causing the invalid memchr read."
  },
